				<table border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="1" bgcolor="#6394BD" class="bordercolor">
					<tr>
						<td align="left" bgcolor="#6E94B7" class="titlebg"><font class="text1" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">&nbsp;5&nbsp;</font></td>
						<td width="75%" bgcolor="#6E94B7" class="titlebg"><font class="text1" color="#FFFFFF" size="2"><b>&nbsp;General Category / General Discussion / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1;action=display;threadid=637;start=msg5449#msg5449" style="color: #FFFFFF">Re:First Impression of GoD?</a></b></font></td>
						<td align="right" bgcolor="#6E94B7" class="titlebg" nowrap="nowrap"><font class="text1" color="#FFFFFF" size="2">&nbsp;on: <b>Today</b> at 05:41:34pm&nbsp;</font></td>
					</tr><tr>
						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#DEE7EF" class="catbg"><font class="catbg" size="2">Started by <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=viewprofile;user=Kinladar">Kinladar</a> | Last post by <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=viewprofile;user=Callon">Callon</a></font></td>
					</tr><tr>
						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#F8F8F8" valign="top" height="40" class="windowbg2">Initial impression:&nbsp; Blows.&nbsp; Hard.&nbsp; Swallows.<br /><br />2nd zone... tiny thing that is mostly a connector to 3 harder zones.&nbsp; It has a big blue dome in the middle.&nbsp; My group fought here for awhile.&nbsp; Mobs were fairly easy... conned blue... hit for 430 or so... 510dd proc.&nbsp; Some had an annoying special ability that I&#039;ll call &quot;the devs hate meleers&quot;.&nbsp; The mob would be &quot;surrounded by a dark aura&quot; when it got down to 20-30% health.&nbsp; This made all melee damage totally suck... like 1/5th or less of it&#039;s usual output.&nbsp; We didn&#039;t see any loot to speak of on the mobs.&nbsp; Then we learned they conned L57 or less.&nbsp; Experience was awful and these mobs are definitely undercons.&nbsp; We moved on to the temple of something or other.<br /><br />The temple really sucked.&nbsp; All the yard trash hit for around 1k.&nbsp; We pushed in fairly deep before we made one small mistake and wiped.&nbsp; Went back... many mobs see invis, so scratch that for CRs.&nbsp; We got an sos rogue friend to go in.&nbsp; He gave up after a couple deaths.&nbsp; Some mobs there see through sos.&nbsp; So basically to CR here you need a necro or SK.&nbsp; Lame.&nbsp; We killed steadily for an hour, hour and a half maybe... no loot and no mobs spotted except the same trash we saw at the front of the zone.&nbsp; Wheeeee... did I mention it sucked?&nbsp; It wasn&#039;t even remotely worth the high risk level.&nbsp; <br /><br />We finally got CR&#039;ed when a raid from Ascent and some people from EiE/DA were CRing themselves.&nbsp; They had some people kill things up front and their rogues eventually got us to the zone and rezzed.&nbsp; <br /><br />Thanks to Meff, Dreadspirit (deadspirit?), and any other rogues that helped and Jaspyr from Ascent for rezzing my group.&nbsp; We were extremely frustrated by that time and it was much appreciated to have someone bail us out.&nbsp; <br /><br />So the age of the horrible, long, mindnumbingly boring CR is back with GoD.&nbsp; /rude Sony&nbsp; I&#039;ve heard that the gravedigger in that first Court of whateveritscalled zone is supposed to be able to summon your corpse from other zones for you.&nbsp; Well, if so he&#039;s also broken right now.&nbsp; He&#039;ll only summon your corpse if it&#039;s in that zone... which is a tiny zone anyway.&nbsp; <br /><br />Moving on... the tribute system is idiotic right now.&nbsp; It&#039;s giving out huge points for fine steel and similar trash drops from other zones.&nbsp; People are AEing solA to cart bags full of FS back to the their temples and getting over 1k points per piece.&nbsp; Now people can fight over all the crap loot we usually let rot.&nbsp; Sweet.&nbsp; And we get to clear a bunch of space in our backpacks for this garbage and make frequent trips back to the hometown temple.&nbsp; WTF... I never wanted to see that backwater sewer called Qeynos again.&nbsp; <br /><br />AA costs are obscene.&nbsp; These AA are apparently designed for the 2% or so of the playerbase that has 400+ AA points and plays an enormous amount so they don&#039;t know what else to do with their points.&nbsp; As an example, the 5 levels of sturdiness cost 4/8/12/16/20 for a total of 60AA points.<br /><br />Rumors of mobs that are highly resistant to some weapons and more vulnerable to others -- this is just plain annoying.&nbsp; Now not only do i have to haul around a good dual wield combo and a good 2 hander... now I&#039;m supposed to carry around good slashers, good blunts, good piercers, etc.&nbsp; </td>
					</tr><tr>
						<td colspan="3" bgcolor="#DEE7EF" class="windowbg"><font size="2">
						&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1;action=post;threadid=637;start=5;title=Post+reply"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/reply_sm.gif" alt="Reply" title="Reply" border="0" /></a> <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1;action=post;threadid=637;quote=5449;title=Post+reply;sesc=1fb0d3d1cf3bb3a7d22166ba07f07362"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a> <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1;action=notify;threadid=637;start=5"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/notify_sm.gif" alt="Notify of replies" title="Notify of replies" border="0" /></a>
						</font></td>
